  "narrative": "All estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed evidence supports the claimed direction and negative signed evidence opposes it. The direct adult-category robustness tests for the three core predictors are unambiguous. H33 gives SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA4-intact adult samples +0.827 [0.750, 0.904] in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. H34 gives TP53-loss versus TP53-intact adult samples +0.453 [0.345, 0.561] in the claimed weaker-dependency direction. H70 gives KEAP1-loss versus KEAP1-intact adult samples +0.827 [0.750, 0.904] in the claimed weaker-dependency direction. In each case, the point estimate and interval lower bound exceed the 0.15-unit scientific-effect threshold. I accept all three direct adult-category contrasts and close them as within-dataset robustness results: the core associations are not confined to the dominant adenocarcinoma subtype or to the overall unstratified population, but also retain substantive magnitude in adult samples. These remain marginal associations in the supplied dataset and do not adjust for other predictors or establish causality.\n\nThe PTEN-loss context-robustness interactions are less conclusive. H89, the Avana-library interaction, gives +0.199 [-0.089, 0.486]. The point estimate is above the threshold and supports the claimed direction, but the interval includes zero and values well below threshold, largely because only 27 PTEN-loss non-Avana samples contribute to the complement. I leave H89 unresolved and defer it: the result is suggestive of possible Avana-specific amplification but is too imprecise to claim, and further small library-restricted cuts are unlikely to be informative without independent data. H90, the adult-category interaction, gives +0.127 [-0.103, 0.357]. The point estimate is below threshold and the interval is wide, including both meaningful amplification and no meaningful modification. I leave H90 unresolved and deferred for the same reason: the adult direct effect H34 is accepted, but the formal interaction is too imprecise to conclude context-specific modification. H91, the high-serum interaction, gives -0.063 [-0.266, 0.141]. The signed estimate is opposite the claimed PTEN-loss amplification in high-serum samples, and the interval upper bound is below the 0.15 threshold. I reject and close H91: the present evidence does not support a scientifically meaningful amplification of the PTEN-loss association in the 10%-serum subgroup. The interval also crosses zero, so this is not sufficient evidence to register a reversed attenuation claim without a new hypothesis.\n\nThe broad discovery probes are mostly negative except for a strong reversal. H98 BRAF V600E, claimed in the stronger-dependency direction, gives +0.049 [-0.071, 0.169]. The point estimate is far below threshold and includes zero, so I reject and close it as unsupported. H100 has_rna_omics availability, a technical/completeness probe rather than a biological hypothesis, gives -0.028 [-0.117, 0.062], rejecting and closing any meaningful RNA-assay-availability difference at the pre-specified threshold. H38 marker E and H39 marker F give near-null signed estimates, -0.021 [-0.080, 0.039] and -0.035 [-0.094, 0.025] respectively, opposing their registered positive directions and comfortably below threshold in magnitude. I reject and close both constructed marker assays as unsupported. H63, media 10% versus 2%, gives +0.012 [-0.072, 0.095], below threshold with an upper bound below threshold, so I reject and close this broader media contrast. Together these nulls strengthen the conclusion that the core genetic predictors and the newly identified MSI-high signal are the salient within-dataset associations among the tested predictors.\n\nThe major new finding is H99, MSI-high registered in the weaker-dependency direction. The signed estimate is -0.792 [-0.907, -0.676], meaning MSI-high samples have raw composite scores approximately 0.79 units more negative than non-MSI-high samples, corresponding to stronger composite dependency. The original H99 claim is therefore decisively rejected: the point estimate and interval are not merely below the threshold in the claimed direction but are strongly in the opposite direction. The magnitude is also large relative to the outcome standard deviation and far exceeds the 0.15-unit threshold in the raw stronger-dependency direction. I register a new reversed mean-difference claim for msi_high in the stronger-dependency direction, linked to H99 and motivated by R88. I set its initial status to accept as a within-dataset marginal association because the evidence is large, precise, and internally coherent, but I explicitly qualify this as an unadjusted association. MSI-high may be confounded with lineage subtype, mutation burden, core alterations, or a coding/indicator anomaly, and this is a composite dependency endpoint rather than a DNA-repair-specific knockout phenotype. Therefore the claim should not be interpreted as causal or biologically specific at this stage.\n\nI request independent validation of H99 rather than a claim that has already been independently validated or a small underpowered PTEN context. Although H99 is the original weaker-dependency claim, validation of that same comparison will test the raw MSI-high contrast under independent sampling and independent interval correction. Because the validation estimate will be signed to the original H99 direction, a negative signed validation result would further support the rejected original direction and the reversed stronger-dependency interpretation. This is the most valuable validation now available: it addresses an unexpected large new association, where false positives, indicator miscoding, or subgroup enrichment are plausible competing explanations, while avoiding redundant validation of the already established core predictors. I keep H99 active pending that validation response. I defer the remaining core subtype and library/adult interaction claims H82-H84 and H92-H97 because direct robustness estimates for the core predictors are already accepted and the interactions would require meaningful modification effects beyond 0.15 units; unless validation or future context analyses reveal important heterogeneity, those tests are less informative than following up the MSI-high signal.",
  "research_notes": "Round 7 appraise. Accepted core within-dataset predictors remain SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, TP53 loss weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss weaker dependency, and PTEN loss stronger dependency. New direct adult robustness tests accepted and closed: SMARCA4 adult +0.827 [0.750,0.904]; TP53 adult +0.453 [0.345,0.561]; KEAP1 adult +0.827 [0.750,0.904]. PTEN context interactions: Avana +0.199 [-0.089,0.486] unresolved/deferred due small non-Avana cell; adult +0.127 [-0.103,0.357] unresolved/deferred; high-serum -0.063 [-0.266,0.141] rejected/closed. Broad probes rejected/closed: BRAF +0.049 [-0.071,0.169]; has_rna -0.028 [-0.117,0.062]; marker E -0.021 [-0.080,0.039]; marker F -0.035 [-0.094,0.025]; media 10 vs 2 +0.012 [-0.072,0.095]. Major discovery: MSI-high registered weaker direction gives -0.792 [-0.907,-0.676], strongly opposite original. Original H99 rejected but active pending validation. Proposed reversed MSI-high stronger-dependency claim direction -1, parent H99, initial accept as marginal within-dataset association. Requested validation H99 to test same raw contrast independently and guard against coding/confounding; negative signed validation supports reversed interpretation. Defer H82-H84 and H92-H97 core interactions. Next: assess H99 validation; if supported, follow MSI-high in contexts/clean backgrounds/subtypes/with core predictors, while interpreting as unadjusted association. Avoid additional low-power small PTEN cuts unless a strong reason emerges.",
